      "side": 1,
      "message": "I ended up making this change on a hunch (and sure enough it turned out to be necessary). Even though the struct member declaration for `S::a` does not have an address space qualifier, the qualifier is somehow retained on the field type depending on the constructor. I imagine there is some interesting type expansion going on under the hood but I can only guess at it.\n\nEither way, this test passes when we use `make_array_ref` in the struct comparison functions and fails if we don\u0027t.",
